e:T2f18,<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">AFROSON1C X (AFX), West Africa&rsquo;s premier platform for music, innovation, and cultural exchange, returns to Accra on Saturday, 10 January 2026 at Treehouse Restaurant, Nyaniba.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Following acclaimed international showcases at SXSW London and Reeperbahn Festival in 2025, AFX returns home with a clear mission: to connect the global creative ecosystem with the next wave of West African talent, ideas and influence.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Produced by the team that has brought major international acts such as GRAMMY Award-winner PJ Morton of Maroon 5 and Denzel Curry to Ghana, AFX continues to solidify Accra&rsquo;s reputation as one of the world&rsquo;s most exciting hubs for creative discovery.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin-bottom: 4pt; line-height: 1.5; break-after: auto; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Headliner Announcement: The Cavemen.</span></strong></span></h2>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">AFX proudly announces The Cavemen. &mdash; Kingsley &amp; Benjamin Okorie &mdash; as the official headliners for 2026. The Nigerian-born duo are the global torchbearers of modern highlife, blending ancestral rhythms with jazz-infused arrangements and contemporary soul. Their work embodies the AFX mandate: innovation rooted in culture.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Introducing the AFX Legacy Performance: Amakye Dede</span></strong></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">We are proud to announce Amakye Dede in the new AFX Legend Slot &mdash; a moment created to honour the giants who shaped Ghana&rsquo;s musical identity. As we build the future of West African music and culture, it is essential that we honour the past. Amakye Dede&rsquo;s presence bridges generations: a living icon whose highlife legacy continues to influence today&rsquo;s alternative, soul, and afro-fusion artists. His performance is not simply nostalgic &mdash; it is a reminder that the future stands strongest when it is rooted in the greatness that came before.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin-bottom: 4pt; line-height: 1.5; break-after: auto; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">What to Expect at AFX 2026</span></strong></span></h2>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">AFX 2026 is designed as an immersive, high-impact experience for artists, executives, creatives, and industry leaders:</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"><span style="mso-list: Ignore;">●<span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-language-override: normal; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Showcases from 10+ emerging artists</span></strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"> from Ghana, Nigeria and West Africa including Tommy W&Aacute;, 99 Phaces, Mala&iuml;ka, Haeven &amp; Tower with more to be announced<br style="mso-special-character: line-break;"><!-- [if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br style="mso-special-character: line-break;"><!--[endif]--></span></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0in 0in 12pt 0.5in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"><span style="mso-list: Ignore;">●<span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-language-override: normal; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Global industry delegation</span></strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"> including industry executives, A&amp;Rs and founders from Virgin Music Group, Symphonic Distribution, WAVVI, EMPIRE, rain. Labs, CLIP (Creators Learn Intellectual Property) &amp; many more</span></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0in 0in 12pt 0.5in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"><span style="mso-list: Ignore;">●<span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-language-override: normal; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Industry sessions</span></strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">, panels, practical workshops and listening rooms</span></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0in 0in 12pt 0.5in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"><span style="mso-list: Ignore;">●<span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-language-override: normal; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Social-impact programming</span></strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"> focused on sustainability, youth development, and community empowerment</span></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0in 0in 12pt 0.5in; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"><!-- [if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><!--[endif]--></span></span><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;"><span style="mso-list: Ignore;">●<span style="font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-language-override: normal; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">A curated <strong>Music Industry Networking Event</strong> bringing together artists, executives, founders, and industry leaders</span></span></p>
<h2 style="margin-bottom: 4pt; line-height: 1.5; break-after: auto; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">Tickets Now Available</span></strong></span></h2>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Limited <strong>Early Bird Tickets</strong> are available via <strong>Tix Africa via WWW.AFROSON1CX.COM</strong>, starting at <strong>GH₵300.00</strong> for the main showcase on 10 January.<br>Attendees are encouraged to secure passes early as prices will rise in later tiers.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin-bottom: 4pt; line-height: 1.5; break-after: auto; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%;">About AFROSON1C X (AFX)</span></strong></span></h2>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%; color: #242424;">AFROSON1C X</span></strong><span lang="EN" style="line-height: 150%; color: #242424;"> is a pioneering showcase festival and industry conference at the intersection of music, technology, and the arts, launching in Accra, Ghana in January 2026. Dedicated to connecting West African creatives with global opportunities, it curates cutting-edge talent from West Africa for international stages. The festival recently made its international debut with a packed stage at SXSW London, spotlighting emerging artists from Ghana and Nigeria, and also hosted a dedicated stage at the Reeperbahn Festival in Hamburg.</span></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #242424;">Co-founded by British music entrepreneur <strong>Tom Russell</strong> and German-Ghanaian singer-songwriter <strong>Y&rsquo;akoto</strong>, AFROSON1C X brings together two decades of artistic, cultural, and industry expertise. Y&rsquo;akoto &mdash; known for her critically acclaimed albums, global touring career, and her distinctive blend of neo-soul and alternative influences &mdash; has built a reputation as one of the most compelling contemporary live voices in Europe. Her influence spans performance, songwriting, and social commentary, giving AFROSON1C X an authentic artistic foundation rooted in both West African and European creative culture.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN" style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #242424;">Tom Russell &mdash; a former Universal-signed artist with a career spanning live events, cultural philanthropy and artist management across the UK, Australia, and West Africa &mdash; has spent years in Ghana fostering local talent and building platforms for global exposure. Together, Tom and Y&rsquo;akoto are at the forefront of building infrastructure for the next generation of music entrepreneurs and creators, with a growing footprint across Africa, Europe &amp; the US.</span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 1.5; margin: 12pt 0in; text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</p>f:T29cc,<p id="docs-internal-guid-a9d8c2b0-7fff-480e-9b29-5724a84f8849" dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Accra, Ghana &mdash; 12th December 2025: Spirit-filled Ghanaian gospel minstrel Minister Owusua has officially released her highly anticipated new single, &ldquo;Ye Dan Wo (We Depend On You)&rdquo;, a heartfelt worship anthem declaring total reliance on God in times of uncertainty, triumph, and transition.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Written by Eunice Owusua Baah, the song carries a deep prophetic message of surrender, trust, and divine assurance. &ldquo;Ye Dan Wo&rdquo; reminds believers that regardless of life&rsquo;s storms, God remains the ultimate source of strength, direction, and protection.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Stream / Download Ye Dan Wo on preferred music platform&nbsp;</span><a style="text-decoration: none;" href="https://mipromo.lks.to/MinisterOwusua/YeDanWo"><span style="color: #4285f4; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: #e67e23;">HERE!</span></span></a></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Accompanied by a visually captivating music video directed by the renowned David Ashbel, the project delivers a cinematic worship experience that elevates the emotional resonance of the song. The video captures Minister Owusua&rsquo;s passionate ministration, drawing listeners and viewers into a deeply personal place of communion with God.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Speaking about the inspiration behind the song, Minister Owusua expressed that &ldquo;Ye Dan Wo is more than music &mdash; it is a prayer, a declaration, and a reminder that we depend on God for everything. My desire is that this song revives faith, strengthens weary hearts, and turns the attention of the world back to Jesus.&rdquo;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><iframe style="border-radius: 12px;" src="https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/6UQ4FSTzyXtnbAweuvOCxW?utm_source=generator" width="100%" height="352" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" loading="lazy" data-testid="embed-iframe"></iframe></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">With its powerful vocals, moving instrumentation, and spirit-led message, &ldquo;Ye Dan Wo (We Depend On You)&rdquo; is poised to become a favourite among worshippers, churches, and gospel music lovers across the nation and beyond.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The song is now available on all digital streaming platforms, with the official music video streaming on YouTube.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Stream / Download Ye Dan Wo on preferred music platform&nbsp;</span><a style="text-decoration: none;" href="https://mipromo.lks.to/MinisterOwusua/YeDanWo"><span style="color: #4285f4; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: #e67e23;">HERE!</span></span></a></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">About Minister Owusua</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Minister Owusua is a rising Ghanaian gospel artist known for her anointed worship ministry, soul-stirring vocals, and passion for leading believers into deep encounters with God through music. Her ministry continues to touch countless lives through spirit-led worship, uplifting messages, and impactful music releases.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><a href="https://youtu.be/ptSat_t2Bj8" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: #e67e23;">Watch official music video for &ldquo;Ye Dan Wo&rdquo;</span></span></a></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Get interactive with Minister Owusua via:</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Instagram:&nbsp;</span><span style="color: #e67e23;"><a style="text-decoration: none; color: #e67e23;" href="https://instagram.com/ministerowusua"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">@ministerowusua</span></a></span></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 1.5;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">TikTok:<span style="color: #e67e23;">&nbsp;</span></span><a style="text-decoration: none;" href="https://www.tiktok.com/@ministerowusua/"><span style="color: #4285f4; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: #e67e23;">@ministerowusua</span></span></a></span></p>10:T3a21,<p id="docs-internal-guid-4be1bba0-7fff-802b-a2a1-45e3a075ff83" dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: -0.098999pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.098999pt; margin: 0pt 10.3588pt 0pt -0.098999pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Accra, Ghana </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ndash; As the year draws to a close, Ghanaian singer and songwriter &ldquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">RAEVIN&rdquo; </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">returns with a powerful reimagining of one of his standout records, titled </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;PIANO II,&rdquo; </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">featuring &ldquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">RCEE&rdquo; </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">and &ldquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">JUBED&rdquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">. The song officially drops on </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">December 17, 2025</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">, serving as Raevin&rsquo;s final release of the year.&nbsp;</span></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: -0.275002pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.275002pt; margin: 12.5922pt 7.99188pt 0pt 0.450996pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;PIANO II&rdquo; is an evolved version of the original </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;PIANO&rdquo; </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">record, which first appeared on Raevin&rsquo;s well-received </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">FEELINGS OF RAEVIN</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&rdquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">. While the original captured listeners with its raw emotion and melodic honesty, this new version expands the story, adding fresh perspectives, richer textures, and deeper feeling through carefully chosen collaborations.&nbsp;</span></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: 0.450996pt; margin: 12.5922pt 3.60724pt 0pt 0.396004pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Produced by </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">HYLANDERBEATZ&rdquo;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">, </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;PIANO II&rdquo; blends warm piano chords, subtle rhythms, and soulful melodies, creating a reflective soundscape that speaks to love, vulnerability, and emotional clarity. Rcee and Jubed each bring their own distinct energy to the record, complementing Raevin&rsquo;s expressive delivery and elevating the song into a shared experience rather than a solo confession.</span></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: -0.219994pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.219994pt; margin: 0pt 0.410461pt 0pt 0.495003pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Speaking on the release, Raevin shares that &ldquo;PIANO II&rdquo; is about growth &mdash; not just musically, but emotionally.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: -0.219994pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.219994pt; margin: 0pt 0.410461pt 0pt 0.495003pt; text-align: justify;">&nbsp;</p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: -0.219994pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0.219994pt; margin: 0pt 0.410461pt 0pt 0.495003pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><iframe style="border-radius: 12px;" src="https://open.spotify.com/embed/album/3aAhU8LCGTuDJromnvVZwR?utm_source=generator" width="100%" height="352" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" loading="lazy" data-testid="embed-iframe"></iframe></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: 0.913002pt; margin: 12.5922pt 1.32037pt 0pt 0.461998pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: italic; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&ldquo;The first version was personal. &lsquo;PIANO II&rsquo; is communal. It&rsquo;s about letting other voices help tell the same story from different angles,&rdquo; he says.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 0.0329971pt; text-indent: 0.220001pt; margin-top: 12.5922pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The release marks a fitting close to a year that saw Raevin strengthen his artistic identity, refine his sound, and deepen his connection with listeners. Rather than chasing trends, &ldquo;PIANO II&rdquo; stays rooted in feeling &mdash; a reminder of why Raevin&rsquo;s music continues to resonate with audiences across Ghana and beyond. </span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 0.0329971pt; text-indent: 0.220001pt; margin-top: 12.5922pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><a href="raevin.lnk.to/PianoII"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><span style="color: #e67e23;">Stream Here</span></span></span></a></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 19.2111pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">ABOUT RAEVIN&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; text-indent: 0.737pt; margin: 2.14404pt 14.2288pt 0pt 0.132004pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Raevin is Ghana&rsquo;s newest Afrofusion force, soulful, magnetic, and fearless. Born in Worawora in the Oti Region, his musical journey began in church, where he played drums and trombone and led the choir. He later lent his vocals to King Promise&rsquo;s global smash Terminator, foreshadowing his own breakout moment.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; margin-right: 5.90118pt; text-indent: 0.835999pt; margin-top: 12.5922pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Now signed to Legacy Life Entertainment (in partnership with Crux Global and Sony Music Africa), Raevin is ready to take center stage. His name, derived from the raven, symbolizes transformation, wisdom, and duality. His sound is just as layered, fusing Afrobeats, Afropop, Highlife, and global influences with emotionally rich storytelling.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 0.814003pt; margin-top: 29.6848pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">FOLLOW RAEVIN&rsquo;S JOURNEY&nbsp;</span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 1.023pt; margin-top: 1.70926pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Instagram &ndash;</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"> </span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-skip-ink: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">@iamraevin</span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">&nbsp;</span></span></p>
